luding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 40% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 53% and a beta of 0.98, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.03 vs 5y 0.96), so read it loosely.","About $35.6M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 65% in the 2020 crash and 53% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 21% below its DCF fair value of $22.78, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 9%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $13.64 to $37.66 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 28.9 vs 19.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 42% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.2% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $27.50 on average, 54% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 4% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.17).","It converts 4% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 4.94x.","ROE of 3% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.3x net debt to EBITDA ($38.7M of cash against $236.5M of debt), with interest covered 3.1x.","The current ratio of 0.55 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Goodwill makes up 35% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -0.3% over 3 years and 3.0% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 32% of profits supports about 1.1% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -14.2% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00, a backlog worth 4% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 3%.","Capex runs only 0.8x depreciation (3.7% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 6, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.7%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 1 sale over the past year, net $153K sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.2% (0.2% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 0.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 28.3% of the float, 7.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 13,138 employees, each generates about $151K of revenue, 0.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 4.7% a year.","That works out to $6K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.0M (13x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":52,"head":"Watch: ROIC 3.6% vs WACC 8.9%.","pros":["Trades 21% below fair value of $22.78","Net debt/EBITDA 1.3x","Piotroski F-score 7/9","10 analysts' mean target $27.50 (+54%)"],"cons":["ROIC 3.6% vs WACC 8.9%","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 28.9x vs sector 19.3x","12-1 month momentum -29%"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital","too few checks pass (conviction 52)"],"buy_below":19.36,"vc":{"base":22.78,"base_src":"dcf","bear":13.64,"bull":37.66,"alt_median":4.06,"n_alt":2,"gap":4.612,"dispersion":0.0923,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","DCF is 461% above the other models' median ($4.06)"]},"med":{"pe":19.